      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xspi__intr__example_1ga9311ed4ae1b8862383322e45697ee09c" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int SpiIntrExample</definition>
        <argsstring>(XSpi *SpiInstancePtr, UINTPTR BaseAddress)</argsstring>
        <name>SpiIntrExample</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_spi" kindref="compound">XSpi</ref> *</type>
          <declname>SpiInstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>UINTPTR</type>
          <declname>BaseAddress</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs a minimal test on the Spi device and driver as a design example. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The purpose of the function is to illustrate how to use the <ref refid="struct_x_spi" kindref="compound">XSpi</ref> component using the interrupt mode.</para><para>The function sends data and expects to receive the same data.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">SpiInstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the instance of Spi component. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">BaseAddress</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Base address of the device.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS if successful, XST_DEVICE_NOT_FOUND if the SPI configuration is not found, otherwise XST_FAILURE.</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>- In XSCT/classic flow, the device configuration is looked up by DeviceId.<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>The function contains an infinite loop such that if interrupts are not working it may never return. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
